// Engine message catalogue: canonical Arabic message -> English.
//
// Keys are the engine's own text as written in lib/reconciliation, with each
// template slot written ${…}. In English, {0}, {1}… are the same slots in the
// same order, and the prefix says what the slot holds:
//   {0}   user data (a file, sheet or column name, a reference, an amount):
//         shown exactly as it is, never translated;
//   {e0}  a word the engine chose (a side, "empty"): translated only when it
//         is exactly a catalogue entry;
//   {t0}  text the engine composed (a nested reason or description):
//         translated as a message in its own right.
// tests/i18n-engine-catalog.test.ts scans the engine and fails when a message
// has no English, when an entry no longer exists in the engine, or when the
// slots do not correspond.
